===== mime-declared-on-send (text/plain) =====
leg: mime-declared-on-send
leg-outcome: text/plain
leg-reason: the content type this run declares for the document under test, fixed by FLOW3_DOCUMENT_CONTENT_TYPE so that both captures declare the same thing, recorded verbatim.  Recorded on every path; whether the document was actually sent is stated by the store leg, not by this row
note: this leg is named even though it was not observed, so that the
  status file carries the same token set in both runs and the gap is
  visible in a directory diff rather than being absent from it (R-5).

===== mime-recorded-by-application (text/plain) =====
leg: mime-recorded-by-application
leg-outcome: text/plain
leg-reason: the content type the application persisted FOR THE DOCUMENT, read from the store response body; this is the direct output of the reinstated activation framework MIME mapping and is recorded verbatim, never normalised
note: this leg is named even though it was not observed, so that the
  status file carries the same token set in both runs and the gap is
  visible in a directory diff rather than being absent from it (R-5).

===== mime-resolved-on-download (text/plain;charset=UTF-8) =====
leg: mime-resolved-on-download
leg-outcome: text/plain;charset=UTF-8
leg-reason: the content type the download endpoint declared when serving the same document back; recorded verbatim
note: this leg is named even though it was not observed, so that the
  status file carries the same token set in both runs and the gap is
  visible in a directory diff rather than being absent from it (R-5).

===== store-response-representation-type (application/json;charset=UTF-8) =====
leg: store-response-representation-type
leg-outcome: application/json;charset=UTF-8
leg-reason: the content type of the STORE RESPONSE ITSELF — the endpoint representation format, normally JSON.  Recorded because it is genuine evidence about the endpoint, and DELIBERATELY EXCLUDED from the MIME criterion because it describes the response envelope and not the document
note: this leg is named even though it was not observed, so that the
  status file carries the same token set in both runs and the gap is
  visible in a directory diff rather than being absent from it (R-5).

===== mime-identity (yes) =====
leg: mime-identity
leg-outcome: yes
leg-reason: whether declared, recorded and served named the same media type.  Compared on the media type — type/subtype, lower-cased, parameters removed — because a charset parameter added by the container is not a MIME resolution difference; compared essences were declared=text/plain recorded=text/plain served=text/plain, and every value above is recorded verbatim
note: this leg is named even though it was not observed, so that the
  status file carries the same token set in both runs and the gap is
  visible in a directory diff rather than being absent from it (R-5).

===== mime-resolution (text/plain) =====
leg: mime-resolution
leg-outcome: text/plain
leg-reason: the media type on which declared, recorded and served all agreed; the three verbatim values are recorded in their own rows above
note: this leg is named even though it was not observed, so that the
  status file carries the same token set in both runs and the gap is
  visible in a directory diff rather than being absent from it (R-5).

===== retrieved-bytes-match (yes) =====
leg: retrieved-bytes-match
leg-outcome: yes
leg-reason: whether the bytes retrieved equalled the bytes sent, compared by digest
note: this leg is named even though it was not observed, so that the
  status file carries the same token set in both runs and the gap is
  visible in a directory diff rather than being absent from it (R-5).

